IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — GOAL 3 (PART): RATES.
--
--   "What weekly rate is payable after the income test?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_32.txt — s 17,
-- Schedule 2 (Income Tests 1-4), Schedule 4 Part 2.

§ `Rates`

-- Schedule 2: "Income Test 1 means that the applicable rate of benefit must
-- be reduced— (a) by 30 cents for every $1 of the total income of the
-- beneficiary and the beneficiary's spouse or partner that is more than $160
-- a week but not more than $250 a week; and (b) by 70 cents for every $1 of
-- that income that is more than $250 a week. Income Test 2 ... 15 cents ...
-- 35 cents ... Income Test 3 ... 70 cents for every $1 ... more than ... $160
-- a week. Income Test 4 ... 35 cents for every $1 ... more than $160 a week".
@ref Schedule 2 Income Tests 1-4
@export The weekly reduction of a benefit under the Income Tests in Schedule 2 of the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ), on the total weekly income of the beneficiary and their partner: Income Test 1, 30 cents per dollar from $160 to $250 and 70 cents above; Income Test 2, 15 and 35 cents; Income Test 3, 70 cents above $160; Income Test 4, 35 cents above $160. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS AN `Income test`  @desc The income test
      income IS A NUMBER  @desc The total weekly income of the beneficiary and their spouse or partner
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction under` t `on weekly income of` income MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `Income Test 1` THEN 0.30 TIMES band PLUS 0.70 TIMES above250
    WHEN `Income Test 2` THEN 0.15 TIMES band PLUS 0.35 TIMES above250
    WHEN `Income Test 3` THEN 0.70 TIMES above160
    WHEN `Income Test 4` THEN 0.35 TIMES above160
    WHERE
        above160 MEANS max 0 (income MINUS 160)
        above250 MEANS max 0 (income MINUS 250)
        band MEANS max 0 (min income 250 MINUS 160)

-- s 17(1) "Assistance granted under this Part must be paid at the
-- appropriate rate specified in Schedule 4." Schedule 4 Part 2 "1 To a
-- beneficiary with 1 or more dependent children: $521.52 a week, subject to
-- Income Test 1. 2 For the purposes of clause 1, MSD may disregard up to $20
-- a week of the beneficiary's personal earnings used to meet the cost of
-- childcare". The jobseeker support and supported living payment tables
-- (Parts 1 and 3) are lost in the conversion: the base rate and its income
-- test are inputs. A rate is never below zero.
@ref s 17(1); Schedule 4 Parts 1-3
@export The weekly rate of a main benefit under s 17 and Schedule 4 of the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ) after the income test: for sole parent support, $521.52 less Income Test 1 (with up to $20 of childcare earnings disregarded); for jobseeker support and the supported living payment, the base rate less its income test (both inputs, as the tables are lost in the converted text); never below zero. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Main benefit`  @desc The benefit
      r IS A `Rate facts`  @desc The base rate and income test (for jobseeker support and the supported living payment), weekly income, and childcare earnings
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly rate of` b `, rate facts` r MEANS
    IF   b EQUALS `sole parent support`
    THEN max 0 (521.52 MINUS `the reduction under` `Income Test 1` `on weekly income of` (max 0 (r's `weekly income of the person and partner` MINUS min 20 (r's `earnings used for childcare`))))
    ELSE max 0 (r's `base weekly rate` MINUS `the reduction under` (r's `income test for the rate`) `on weekly income of` (r's `weekly income of the person and partner`))
